Preserve NOMMU mapping ownership when mmap reuses physical addresses.

A Maple Tree slot holds one VMA. Repeated exact mappings previously
replaced an existing VMA and lost its ownership record, leaking file,
region and callback references. Unmapping the replacement also made the
still-live earlier mapping disappear. Chain exact aliases behind the
current slot, pop one mapping per unmap, and release the entire chain on
exit. Retain locks until the last mapping of the range is removed.

Reject nonidentical overlapping ranges before registration rather than
clipping existing VMA records. Enforce the existing max_map_count on new
mappings and expose its sysctl on NOMMU, matching the MMU control. Update
total_vm on unmap and include retained alias metadata in proc accounting.
/proc/PID/maps continues to show each physical address range once.

